id: pm-jev-release-gate
title: Release readiness behind PM_RELEASE_APPROVED
description: "Prepare daily OIDC publishing behind one repository approval variable. Verify metadata, allowlisted packed files, privacy, regression checks, npm and Bun release gates. The owner performs the first npm publish and trusted-publisher setup; keep approval unset."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-25T23:21:14.854Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T09:10:48.474Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-27T09:10:47.578Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-27T04:51:59.000Z"
author: codex-agent
resolution: "Merged PR #51 at a2592c772e12a463ff6a8de10f03abb79b64824c; inspected .github/workflows/release.yml and ran node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/release-approval.test.ts on main. Canonical-repository write guards, main/approval gating, daily schedule and OIDC provenance safeguards are delivered. First publication, trusted-publisher setup and workflow activation remain owner actions; closing repository preparation does not authorize them."
expected_result: "Prepare daily OIDC publishing behind one repository approval variable. Verify metadata, allowlisted packed files, privacy, regression checks, npm and Bun release gates. The owner performs the first npm publish and trusted-publisher setup; keep approval unset."
actual_result: "Canonical-repository write guards, main/approval gating, daily schedule and OIDC provenance safeguards are delivered. First publication, trusted-publisher setup and workflow activation remain owner actions; closing repository preparation does not authorize them."
comments[14]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T23:21:18.069Z",codex-agent,"Normalize daily scheduling and PM_RELEASE_APPROVED job gates while preserving release decisions, generated changelogs and release notes. Verify OIDC publishing without a stored npm token, manifest metadata, packed allowlists and private-data scans. No open homepage/author PR was found during orientation. No publishing, trust setup, approval variable changes or merges are authorized."
  "2026-10-25T23:31:20.653Z",codex-agent,"Pack verification: npm pack --dry-run --json and the actual npm pack --ignore-scripts artifact agree on 106 allowlisted files (calibration: 9; dist: 80; docs: 9; examples: 3; root files: 5). Every packed member was scanned for absolute home paths, npm/GitHub/cloud tokens, private keys, hosted-data locations, private addresses and historical owner email addresses: PASS with zero matches. Regression proof: five independent workflow mutations (approval, provenance, token environment, daily schedule and OR bypass) plus the original manifest each fail the new contract check; restored contract passes 4/4. The linked test also passes through pm test --run --progress. Next gates: npm run release:check and bun run release:check with isolated HOME and Git configuration."
  "2026-10-25T23:36:23.854Z",codex-agent,"Full local gates PASS: npm run release:check and bun run release:check, each with isolated HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1. Suite receipts: npm: 1/331 tests; bun: 1/331 tests. No thresholds were relaxed. The package remains unpublished and the approval variable unset; first publication requires the owner login and initial trusted-publisher registration. For the local first publish, explicitly override provenance with --provenance=false because publishConfig enables provenance for cloud CI. CI must confirm the final PR head. The tracker item stays in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-26T01:36:49.281Z",codex-agent,"Read-only GitHub workflow inspection found release.yml manually disabled. Added a narrowly scoped setup workflow that runs on main when release workflow files change (or on manual main dispatch), verifies the existing approval/provenance/manifest contract, confirms main has not advanced, and only then enables release.yml. It never publishes, configures npm trust or changes a repository variable. This activates the guarded schedule automatically after the owner merges, without enabling the older main workflow now. Missing the setup workflow or removing its main-only guard fails the regression; restored check passes 1/1."
  "2026-10-27T00:08:13.940Z",codex-agent,"Review follow-up: preserve existing release-readiness work and merged main changes. Remove automatic release-workflow enablement; the orchestrator enables disabled schedules after merge. Require the canonical repository at job level for every write-permission or publishing job in the affected workflows, alongside the existing approval and branch conditions. Prove guard, approval, provenance and token regressions independently, then wait for complete npm and Bun CI on the pushed head."
  "2026-10-27T00:08:20.332Z",codex-agent,The existing release-workflow regressions also assert exact job conditions. Extend those assertions with the canonical-repository predicate while retaining the existing release decisions and approval checks; keep the file linked as regression evidence.
  "2026-10-27T00:08:51.134Z",codex-agent,"Packed-artifact verification: 106 allowlisted files; dry-run and actual archive agree, and every packed member has zero private-data findings. Local project health passes with extensions disabled; globally installed extension version skew is outside this package."
  "2026-10-27T00:08:52.592Z",codex-agent,"Fork-exclusion revert proof: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/release-approval.test.ts passes 6/6. Independently reverting each job repository guard, reverting all repository guards, allowing an OR bypass, removing approval or provenance, injecting a synthetic npm token environment, adding an unguarded CI write job, inheriting CI write permissions, adding a read-permission CI publisher, and restoring automatic setup all fail (each command exits nonzero; 12 independent mutations rejected). Restoring the workflows passes 6/6. Linked pm tests, test typecheck where present and lint pass. Canonical-repository checks include inherited permissions. Disabled release workflows remain for the orchestrator to enable after merge; no live settings or publishing were changed."
  "2026-10-27T00:27:49.803Z",codex-agent,"A final origin/main refresh added the merged calibration-drift feature. Merge that main update without changing the release guards, preserving both release-activation documentation and calibration documentation. Re-run linked workflow checks, changelog verification and the actual packed-artifact scan, then verify complete CI on the new pushed head. The existing independent workflow revert proof is unchanged."
  "2026-10-27T00:28:11.173Z",codex-agent,"After merging the latest calibration main update, linked workflow tests pass and CHANGELOG.md is regenerated and current. The refreshed actual tarball has 127 allowlisted files, matches the dry-run inventory, and has zero private-data findings. Approval and fork-exclusion workflow bytes and the 12 independent revert proofs are unchanged. Complete npm and Bun CI must verify the new merge head."
  "2026-10-27T03:17:21.417Z",codex-agent,"Independent re-review found the contract covered only release and CI files, missing CodeQL security-events writes, owner-only Dependabot guards and reusable workflow callers. Extend canonical-repository guards to every effectively write-enabled job in every workflow file. Replace regex workflow parsing with a pinned YAML parser, generic permission inheritance and negative fixtures for this full class. Correct local publishing documentation, preserve earlier readiness work, prove source reverts and wait for npm/Bun CI on every final head."
  "2026-10-27T03:49:33.926Z",codex-agent,"Whole-workflow contract passes 30/30 using the pinned YAML parser. It scans every YAML workflow, resolves aliases/flow maps, applies job permission overrides or workflow inheritance, and recognizes any scope with write plus write-all, including reusable callers. Negative fixtures cover CodeQL, owner-only/wrong-repository Dependabot, inherited writes, reusable calls, write-all, future scopes, missing publication approval/provenance, provenance overrides, token environments, OR/negation bypasses and discovery of a new workflow in a non-Git directory. Behavioural revert proof: all 14 independent mutations fail with assertion failures: each write job loses only its repository guard, owner-only/OR guards return, approval/provenance disappear, a synthetic token environment is added, file discovery is narrowed back to release/CI, permission matching returns to a scope allowlist, or inheritance is removed. Restoring the implementation passes 30/30. Linked pm tests and the repository's defined typecheck, lint and duplication checks pass. Maintainer local publishing is authenticated and checked, with no approval-variable hold; the variable gates automated GitHub releases."
  "2026-10-27T09:10:41.751Z",codex-agent,"Closure audit: verify every acceptance criterion on current main against merged PR #51 (a2592c772e12a463ff6a8de10f03abb79b64824c), inspect .github/workflows/release.yml, and run the focused linked check before closing. Completion will be the merge timestamp 2026-10-27T04:51:59Z."
  "2026-10-27T09:10:46.838Z",codex-agent,"Merged PR #51 at a2592c772e12a463ff6a8de10f03abb79b64824c; inspected .github/workflows/release.yml and ran node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/release-approval.test.ts on main. Canonical-repository write guards, main/approval gating, daily schedule and OIDC provenance safeguards are delivered. First publication, trusted-publisher setup and workflow activation remain owner actions; closing repository preparation does not authorize them. Full unchanged npm and Bun release gates run in CI for this tracker-only closure PR; prior behavioral revert evidence remains in the merged implementation history."
